🚀 Pro-Level Breakdownjavascriptserver.get('/about', (req, res) => {
    res.send('About Route');
})
Use code with caution.1. server.get (The HTTP Method Listener)What it is: Ye server ko bata raha hai ki hame sirf GET Request ko sunna (listen karna) hai.Pro Concept: HTTP protocol me alag-alag methods hote hain (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE). GET ka kaam hota hai server se data "read" ya "fetch" karna. Agar koi browser me ://yoursite.com likh kar enter marega, toh browser default me ek GET request bhejta hai. Agar koi is page par POST request bhejega, toh ye code execute nahi hoga.2. '/about' (The URI/Path)What it is: Ye endpoints ka address hai.Pro Concept: Isko Routing bolte hain. Server ke paas hazaron files ho sakti hain, lekin ye specific code block tabhi chalega jab request ka URL path exact /about match karega.3. (req, res) => { ... } (The Middleware / Callback Function)What it is: Ye ek Arrow Function hai jo tab trigger hota hai jab upar ka Method aur Path match ho jata hai. Isme do sabse zaroori objects hote hain: req (Request) aur res (Response).Pro Concept:req (Incoming Stream): Isme user/client ki saari kundli hoti hai. Jaise ki unka IP address, browser ka naam (User-Agent), cookies, headers, aur query parameters (?search=node).res (Outgoing Stream): Ye server ka tool hai client ko jawab bhejne ke liye. Iske bina browser ghumta rahega aur timeout ho jayega.4. res.send('About Route') (The Response Payload)What it is: Ye client (browser) ko 'About Route' text bhej raha hai.Pro Concept (Under the Hood): Express.js ka res.send() piche se bohot saara "magic" karta hai jo core Node.js me khud likhna padta:Ye automatic check karta hai ki aap kya bhej rahe ho (String, Object, ya Buffer).Agar aap String bhej rahe ho, toh ye automatic HTTP Header me Content-Type: text/html set kar deta hai.Ye text ki length nikal kar Content-Length header bhi khud set karta hai.Ye HTTP Status Code ko automatic 200 OK set karta hai, jiska matlab hai "Sab sahi chal raha hai".Aur aakhiri me, ye network connection ko safe tarike se close (res.end()) kar deta hai.🧠 Ek Real-World Analogy (Dukan aur Guard)Maan lo aap ek badi dukan (Server) me gaye:server.get: Dukan ka ek counter hai jo sirf "Samaan Dikhane" (GET) ke liye hai, "Samaan Lene" (POST) ke liye nahi.'/about': Us counter ke upar ek board laga hai: "About Section".req: Aap counter ke employee ko ek parchi dete ho jisme aapka naam aur details hain.res.send('About Route'): Employee parchi padhta hai, dukan ke box se 'About Route' naam ka samaan nikaalta hai, use sahi packet me pack karta hai (Headers), aur aapko dekar bolta hai "Thank You, Agli baar aana!"